hod is **unstable** for step size $Δx = 0.25$.\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by $y_{n + 1} = R(λΔx)y_{n}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228074} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228075} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228076} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228077} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228078}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228073}] :question/math-academy-id "q-332571" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation $y^{′} = - λy$ with $y = y(x), y(0) = 1, x \\ge 0, λ = 3$, and step size $Δx$?\n\n1. The stability function is $R(3Δx) = \\frac{1 - 3Δx/2}{1 + 3Δx/2}$.\n2. The stability region is $\\mid \\frac{9}{2}(Δx - \\frac{2}{3})^{2} + \\frac{1}{2} \\mid < 1$.\n3. The method is absolutely stable.\n4. The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx = 2.5$.\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by $y_{n + 1} = R(λΔx)y_{n}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306052} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306393} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306555} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306596} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307167} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307682}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333546" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the implicit Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =6,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(6Δx)=\\frac{1}{1-6Δx}.$\n- The stability region is $|\\frac{1}{1+6Δx}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=0.10.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305350} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305670} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305843} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306089} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305670} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307737}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333572" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=2,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =5,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(5Δx)=\\frac{1-5Δx/2}{1+5Δx/2}.$\n- The stability region is $|\\frac{2-5Δx}{2+5Δx}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=1.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305265} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306174} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306912} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306965} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305265} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308211}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333574" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =2,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(2Δx)=\\frac{1-Δx}{1+Δx}.$\n- The stability region is $|2{(Δx-1)}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=2.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308467 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305409} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305934} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306481} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306778} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307459} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307529}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333578" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the trapezoidal method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=2,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =7,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(7Δx)=\\frac{1+7Δx/2}{1-7Δx/2}.$\n- The stability region is $|\\frac{2-7Δx}{2+7Δx}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305609} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306603} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306750} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306920} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, III, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306603} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307668}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333930" :question/problem "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =4,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(4Δx)=1-4Δx+8(Δx)^{2}.$\n- The stability region is $|8{(Δx-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is stable for step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, III, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305308} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305814} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305884} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307461} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307509} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307802}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333968" :question/problem "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =2,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(2Δx)=1-2Δx+2(Δx)^{2}.$\n- The stability region is $|2{(Δx-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is stable for step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372643} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372644} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372645} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372646} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372647} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372642}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333551" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the implicit Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =1,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+Δx}.$\n- The stability region is $|\\frac{1}{1+Δx}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=0.50.$\n\n*Hint:* The stabili